  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header reveal">
        <span class="section-tag">Why Zanzibar's Spices Matter</span>
        <h2>Historical Significance</h2>
        <p>Zanzibar's spice trade dates back centuries, earning the island the nickname "The Spice Island." The aromatic legacy introduced by Arab and Portuguese traders created a cultural fusion that continues to define Zanzibar's identity today. Spice farming remains a vital part of local life and agriculture.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="highlights-grid">
        <div class="highlight-item reveal">
          <h3>Cloves</h3>
          <p>Zanzibar produces some of the world's finest cloves. Visit a working spice farm to learn about cultivation, harvesting, and the economic importance of this precious spice to the island's history.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="highlight-item reveal delay-2">
          <h3>Vanilla</h3>
          <p>Introduced from Mexico, vanilla thrives in Zanzibar's tropical climate. Discover the labor-intensive process of vanilla bean production and its value in local and international markets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="highlight-item reveal delay-3">
          <h3>Cinnamon & Nutmeg</h3>
          <p>Authentic cinnamon and nutmeg grown on family farms. Learn about the difference between true cinnamon and common varieties, and the traditional uses of nutmeg in Zanzibari cuisine and medicine.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

